  DESIGN CALLS (named, per PACKET.md autonomy):
    1. Label side = the asset's label-visible ASSERTIONS, not the denormalised asset columns.
       Both commit paths (`_create_asset_for_candidate`, `asset_service.create_asset`) write a
       `display_name` assertion beside the column, so production assets always carry one; the
       column's `display_name` still feeds the query name via `read_asset_identifiers`. Reading
       the column would double-count and would invalidate the SG-098/102 fixtures (which seed
       assertions only). F-SG103-3.
    2. `brand` is not label-visible (absent from `LABEL_VISIBLE_FIELDS`; no web path emits it),
       so the conflict is on `display_name` (label assertion) vs the web `display_name`. F-SG103-4.
    3. Label values are provenance envelopes (not bare scalars) so the merged field keeps a
       `value`/`source_type` shape; this also keeps the pre-existing SG-098 `.value` assertion
       valid with no test churn.

